sarah: Quick heads-up — opened a tiny PR for the Error Handbook: compact section that covers 429s, timeouts, context-limit fallbacks and a short JS SDK snippet. PTAL when you have a minute: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/482

ekaterina: Thanks — will review today. Quick skim: love the flow but the JS example has no retry/backoff or Retry-After handling. We should show a safe default.

ben: Also we should call out the recommended behavior for context-limit fallbacks: try prefix trim -> route to shorter model -> if still 429, surface a clear UX error. We have routing docs but not linked here.

sarah: Good call. My plan: add (1) try/catch + exponential backoff snippet for JS, (2) tiny example of trimming context before the call, (3) link to routing policies. Any wording preferences? Keep it short.

ekaterina: For wording: 429 should be called "rate-limited (429)" and mention Retry-After header explicitly. Example: when header present, use that value before retrying; otherwise use exponential backoff with jitter. Remove phrasing like "retry forever".

ben: Could we add a one-paragraph troubleshooting checklist under the snippet? e.g., bullets: probable cause -> immediate action -> follow-up. Don't make a huge table — just 3 bullets.

sarah: Yep — I'll add a 3-bullet checklist. Also adding small troubleshooting CLI snippet to query request logs: `curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" https://api.redwood.ai/v1/logs?request_id=...`

ekaterina: Tiny nit: the routing link anchor in your PR points to `#routing` but the doc anchor is `#routing-policies`. Can you fix the anchor and add a short parenthetical about when to prefer model routing vs capacity fallback?

sarah: Fixed both in the branch and pushed. I also replaced the naive `await client.generate(...)` sample with this:```js
// simple retry with exponential backoff + Retry-After
async function safeGenerate(client, opts) {
  const maxAttempts = 4;
  for (let i = 0; i < maxAttempts; i++) {
    try {
      return await client.generate(opts);
    } catch (err) {
      const retryAfter = parseInt(err.headers?.['retry-after'] || '0', 10);
      if (retryAfter) {
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, retryAfter * 1000));
      } else if (i < maxAttempts - 1) {
        const backoff = Math.min(1000 * 2 ** i + Math.floor(Math.random() * 300), 8000);
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff));
      } else {
        throw err;
      }
    }
  }
}
```

ekat: Looks good, thanks. Can you add one line explaining why we prefer trimming the prompt prefix vs dropping messages? e.g., "prefer selective prefix trimming (system + recent user messages kept) to preserve safety/context."

sarah: Added that line and the 3-bullet checklist: "Cause: bursty traffic / long contexts; Immediate action: implement retry with Retry-After + trim oldest non-essential messages; Follow-up: add prompt set to evals to catch regressions."

